      "text_raw": "Another advantage of deal-\ning with IM is that it also\n3\ngives the third-order cross-\nmodulation CM . Cross-\n3\nmodulation is what we are\nreally after, as it describes\nhow much modulation\ninformation is transferred\nfrom one carrier to its adja-\ncent carrier.\nApplication of an ampli-\ntude modulated waveform\nwith modulation index m\nc\nto the same power series,\nshows that the CM is\n3\nsimply the product of the\nIM with the modulation index m . This is also true to some extent for other modulation systems.\n3 c\nThere are plenty of reasons to concentrate on the IM as the most important specification of\n3\nthird-order distortion.",
